Well, if you navigate using the hjklyunb keys
instead of the number-pad, you can save a keystroke
there, "9s" then suffices. It's also _far_ safer to
do that numbered search than to just lean on the "s"
key, because numbered searches stop automatically
when something sufficiently interesting happens,
while a long string of queued up auto-typed "s"
keystrokes can leave your PC dead before you can
react.

You're _lots_ better off to search multiple times
before stepping over to search the next chunk of
wall. Doing 9s at each search point then walking,
around the room once, versus doing s then walking,
nine times around the room, makes you walk nine
times as far to do the same amount of searching.

What you're worried about in the situation you
describe includes starving, of course, so minimizing
the turns you use is an important part of any
strategy. Don't do all your searching in one room,
and don't search one room at a time for the worst
case number of searches balance your searching among
the known rooms (and corridors), come back and do it
again if the first set of tries fails.

